00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:53.390
And most of the corporations
in the beginning that I got in

00:10:53.390 --> 00:10:57.040
I would either with the
president or the head of HR, your

00:10:57.040 --> 00:11:00.400
you know, your chief
human resource officer

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:03.237
or someone accountable
for marketing, I go,

00:11:03.237 --> 00:11:05.680
"Let me give you 30 minutes or an hour.

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:09.030
You see, and then tell me
if you want to bring us in."

00:11:09.030 --> 00:11:09.906
So we-

00:11:09.906 --> 00:11:11.270
- Stay there for a second.

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:14.060
One thing that I hear
a lot about is people

00:11:15.260 --> 00:11:17.870
demonizing free work.

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:19.770
And, and you just, you don't put it

00:11:19.770 --> 00:11:21.610
on a pedestal, curious to, you know,

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:24.450
I'm sure you've seen this
over the last five to seven,

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:25.370
10, 15 years.

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:26.580
There's a lot of conversations like

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:29.520
never do spec work, never do free work.

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:31.760
It doesn't seem like, you
know, I'm not on that camp.

00:11:31.760 --> 00:11:32.593
- Yeah, no.

00:11:32.593 --> 00:11:33.940
If you're 25-years-old

00:11:33.940 --> 00:11:36.940
and you say you have a product that rocks

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:39.170
and you want in my business?

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:40.370
I'm not going to pay for it.

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:42.700
I don't know you, you
don't come with anything.

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:44.340
So give me a trial.

00:11:44.340 --> 00:11:47.220
And then if I love it, I'm
gonna, I'm going to want it.

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:48.880
I'm going to tell my
other people about it.

00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:49.790
So we were never-

00:11:49.790 --> 00:11:51.000
- And what do you say to people-

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:51.930
- And that's how I got

00:11:51.930 --> 00:11:54.650
some of my biggest NFL players

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:56.480
was like, "Eh, let me give you."

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:57.410
I don't want-

00:11:57.410 --> 00:11:59.470
they all think I'm going
to come for your money.

00:11:59.470 --> 00:12:02.420
No, I'm gonna give you two free sessions.

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:06.890
And if you like what I just
gave you, then you buy.

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:09.220
If you don't like what I gave
you, what's the big deal?

00:12:09.220 --> 00:12:10.560
You got two free sessions.

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:12.240
I met an NFL player.

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:13.240
I made a difference.

00:12:13.240 --> 00:12:14.073
But guess what?

00:12:14.073 --> 00:12:16.100
Every NFL player that I ever gave

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:18.350
two free coaching sessions to?

00:12:18.350 --> 00:12:19.770
My clients.

00:12:19.770 --> 00:12:22.530
- Beth, what about the
people who took free sessions

00:12:22.530 --> 00:12:24.000
and didn't become clients?

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:25.320
What do you say to people-
- God bless!

00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:27.380
I send them away with love.

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:28.980
They don't either have the money.

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:30.610
What I did, they didn't like.

00:12:30.610 --> 00:12:31.443
Who cares?

00:12:31.443 --> 00:12:34.300
That was 30 minutes out
of my frigging life,

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:38.830
maybe an hour out of my entire
life that I gave it away.

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:40.360
I believe it-

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:41.260
Sorry. It's weird.

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:42.970
But I believe in paying it forward.

00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:45.100
You pay it forward, it's coming back.

00:12:45.100 --> 00:12:48.120
Now I don't pay it
forward to 'get it back'.

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:50.300
But why wouldn't I do that?

00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:51.950
Like, if I wanna start in the-

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:54.200
if I wanna build a sports division

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:56.470
and I've never done that before,

00:12:56.470 --> 00:12:57.303
like I could say,

00:12:57.303 --> 00:12:59.960
"Well it translates from
business to sports."

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:03.290
No, I know it does, but
the athlete doesn't.

00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:06.430
So let me just do this for you.

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:09.200
And I, that's how we started
our business and it worked.

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:10.530
And here we are.

00:13:10.530 --> 00:13:13.740
- For the individuals who

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:17.220
who

00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:18.500
have companies.

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:19.333
- Yep.

00:13:19.333 --> 00:13:23.890
- And have six, 12, 22, 212 employees.

00:13:24.750 --> 00:13:28.150
Let's rattle off in this podcast

00:13:28.150 --> 00:13:32.747
themes that you see that are common.

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:35.370
I don't want to say universal

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:36.760
'cause every situation is different

00:13:36.760 --> 00:13:39.660
but there's a lot of commonalities-

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:40.760
- Yep.
- in these things.

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:44.690
What are some of the things
that you see that are common

00:13:44.690 --> 00:13:48.750
in companies that lead to bad cultures

00:13:48.750 --> 00:13:51.057
or vulnerabilities or limited growth or

00:13:51.057 --> 00:13:52.300
(indistinct)

00:13:52.300 --> 00:13:54.760
- Well, I'm going to say one of yours,

00:13:54.760 --> 00:13:56.020
You ready?

00:13:56.020 --> 00:13:56.990
- I'm ready.

00:13:56.990 --> 00:13:57.823
- All right.

00:13:57.823 --> 00:14:00.720
So I know you gave your culture a B minus.

00:14:00.720 --> 00:14:02.340
And so once, you know

00:14:02.340 --> 00:14:04.810
we raised the bar and now it's a B minus.

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:05.730
Okay. Far out.

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:06.810
So then what's in there?

00:14:06.810 --> 00:14:10.560
And so last week, I
did a session with Nick

00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:12.690
and a bunch of his SVPs

00:14:12.690 --> 00:14:16.300
on removing gossip from the workplace.

00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:17.133
- Yep.

00:14:17.133 --> 00:14:20.170
- Gossip is one of the main culprits that

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:25.170
if you do not remove it from
your culture and then put in

00:14:25.730 --> 00:14:28.430
how do you have hard conversations.

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:31.310
So we can talk about client candor

00:14:31.310 --> 00:14:34.400
but you gotta teach people,
how do you do candor?

00:14:34.400 --> 00:14:38.300
Right? Like if I'm not going
to gossip and talk about

00:14:38.300 --> 00:14:41.300
you know, go to somebody
who can't do anything

00:14:41.300 --> 00:14:44.420
about it and tell you crap.

00:14:44.420 --> 00:14:46.480
Right? I gotta take that out.

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:48.420
But then I gotta teach you

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:51.530
go have the courage to
go have the conversation

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:52.850
whether it's with Gary Vee,

00:14:52.850 --> 00:14:56.150
whether it's with this
executive or this person.

00:14:56.150 --> 00:15:00.913
So gossip is one of the main
culprits in an organization.

00:15:01.890 --> 00:15:03.220
- Give me- I love that.

00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:04.250
And I couldn't agree more.

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:05.760
Give me a couple more

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:08.487
because I really want people
to leave here with like,

00:15:08.487 --> 00:15:12.580
"Huh, that is going on
in my shop." You know?

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:13.910
What are-

00:15:13.910 --> 00:15:15.180
Talk to me about-

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:16.013
Actually, let me throw a
couple of things at you.

00:15:16.013 --> 00:15:17.660
And then you'll add.

00:15:17.660 --> 00:15:21.053
What about insecurity of upper management?

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:24.950
When you hear that, how does
that play out in your mind?

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:27.381
- So if someone comes
to me, who's like ins-

00:15:27.381 --> 00:15:32.000
has a whole negative
dialogue about the leadership

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:35.070
before I'm gonna go anywhere
near the leadership,

00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:37.910
You know, I really do
believe in accountability.

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:42.120
So what is this human, why
is this human sitting around

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:45.370
complaining to themselves
and likely other people

00:15:45.370 --> 00:15:47.810
about they're not digging on
the leadership. All right?

00:15:47.810 --> 00:15:50.030
Well what the frick
are you doing about it?

00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:54.120
So I would start with their
being what we call a chicken

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:56.380
and avoiding the conversations.

00:15:56.380 --> 00:15:58.760
I would then help them
to stop being a chicken

00:15:58.760 --> 00:16:01.535
and script the conversation
that they have to

00:16:01.535 --> 00:16:04.460
go have with leadership, right?

00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:08.170
Like, so if you've got your
junior people talking trash

00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:10.750
about the leaders, it's twofold.

00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:12.940
You got junior people being chickens

00:16:12.940 --> 00:16:14.730
not able to go speak to them.

00:16:14.730 --> 00:16:17.060
And then leaders, why do
you have people so scared

00:16:17.060 --> 00:16:19.510
of you that they can't come talk to you?

00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:21.250
So it works both ways.

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:24.300
They don't feel safe enough to go up

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:26.290
and then I'd have to talk to the up-

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:27.280
the leaders - and go,

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:29.450
what are you doing not making
it safe enough for people to

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:31.360
come to you to let you
know what's not working?

00:16:31.360 --> 00:16:35.270
- But from your perspective
all these years, what pers-

00:16:35.270 --> 00:16:36.947
this is such an arbitrary question

00:16:36.947 --> 00:16:38.420
and you'll do your best to answer it.

00:16:38.420 --> 00:16:40.050
But I'm really just fascinated.

00:16:40.050 --> 00:16:42.560
What percentage of companies do you think

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:44.570
are being led by fear?

00:16:44.570 --> 00:16:47.970
And what percentage of companies
do you think are being led

00:16:47.970 --> 00:16:52.130
by optimism and offense and
trying to eliminate fear?

00:16:52.130 --> 00:16:54.900
Just from your perspective
through the years,

00:16:54.900 --> 00:16:58.060
I'm just curious all the
doors that you've walked in-

00:16:58.060 --> 00:17:01.150
- You see, I think no matter
in every company I've been in

00:17:01.150 --> 00:17:03.530
and like I've told you, I
loved that you had created

00:17:03.530 --> 00:17:05.940
in your culture, The Honey Empire, right?

00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:07.220
But we had to deal with that

00:17:07.220 --> 00:17:10.147
it was a lot of honey and not
a lot of, you know, candor.

00:17:10.147 --> 00:17:11.780
- Which, to your point earlier,

00:17:11.780 --> 00:17:13.650
the big breakthrough you've done for

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:17.980
me, which has, is a really
important part like this,

00:17:17.980 --> 00:17:19.850
this term 'kind candor'.

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:22.870
And to your point, now we
have to operationalize it.

00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:25.220
But even in standing up

00:17:25.220 --> 00:17:27.710
and having an entire company
meeting and explaining

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:30.227
to everyone, you know,
back to accountability,

00:17:30.227 --> 00:17:33.410
"Hey, I have very big
ambitions for our culture."

00:17:33.410 --> 00:17:35.750
We've done a lot of
things, right by standards.

00:17:35.750 --> 00:17:37.860
One of the biggest compliments in my

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:40.930
23 years of operating was your assessment

00:17:40.930 --> 00:17:41.763
when you came in and said,

00:17:41.763 --> 00:17:45.130
"Hey, you actually have a lot
of good shit going on here."

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:45.963
You know?

00:17:45.963 --> 00:17:48.360
And our entitlement and our, you know

00:17:48.360 --> 00:17:51.390
my inability and this
always blows my fans' minds.

00:17:51.390 --> 00:17:52.223
I always tell them.

00:17:52.223 --> 00:17:55.330
I'm like, "Public figure
me, great at candor,

00:17:55.330 --> 00:17:57.110
because there's no human
on the other side".

00:17:57.110 --> 00:17:58.740
I'm speaking into truths, right?

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:00.210
I'm speaking on stage.

00:18:00.210 --> 00:18:01.043
- Right.

00:18:01.043 --> 00:18:03.670
- So Gary Vee, brings a
lot of value to people

00:18:03.670 --> 00:18:06.570
candor-wise, but Gary Vaynerchuk the CEO

00:18:07.840 --> 00:18:09.380
really struggled, you know.

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:12.130
And through another part of my life

00:18:12.130 --> 00:18:15.690
I was able to realize
my dad's negative vessel

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:19.639
to delivering candor was
what I was not fond of.

00:18:19.639 --> 00:18:21.620
The energy of the candor

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:24.740
but I had to take years
to separate the vessel

00:18:24.740 --> 00:18:26.090
from the actual thing.

00:18:26.090 --> 00:18:27.240
Candor,

00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:30.050
and the way that I've tried
to position it, kind candor

00:18:30.050 --> 00:18:32.530
I think, is now an essential element

00:18:32.530 --> 00:18:34.483
of our culture and is moving us up.

00:18:35.900 --> 00:18:40.713
We needed that bad, and it's
really made a huge impact,

00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:45.670
but I think it's always
interesting to see what

00:18:45.670 --> 00:18:48.940
commonalities and
shortcomings companies have.

00:18:48.940 --> 00:18:50.235
- Yeah, let me give you another one.

00:18:50.235 --> 00:18:52.700
- Please.
- So another one is,

00:18:52.700 --> 00:18:55.530
and again, in your culture

00:18:55.530 --> 00:18:57.850
and I'm starting to work
on it with your executives

00:18:57.850 --> 00:19:00.270
and will with you in our
coaching session tomorrow

00:19:00.270 --> 00:19:03.340
is that the language of accountability.

00:19:03.340 --> 00:19:06.670
So Gary Vee, you got a language for sure,

00:19:06.670 --> 00:19:08.180
for

00:19:08.180 --> 00:19:09.220
wine, right?

00:19:09.220 --> 00:19:10.520
So like there's languages.

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:12.010
I don't have any language for wine.

00:19:12.010 --> 00:19:13.883
I go, "Hmm, I like it.
Hmm, I don't like it."

00:19:13.883 --> 00:19:16.180
It's the extent of my language.

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:20.270
The language of accountability
is very important.

00:19:20.270 --> 00:19:22.270
In fact, I think that's what'll impact

00:19:22.270 --> 00:19:25.080
the empire side of your Honey Empire.

00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:27.380
What I mean by the
language of accountability

00:19:27.380 --> 00:19:30.640
first and foremost, is the ability

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:34.120
to own when you're not gonna
keep a frigging promise.

00:19:34.120 --> 00:19:38.350
That does not make you
a bad person at all.

00:19:38.350 --> 00:19:43.260
It depends on how you own it
when you just blew a promise.

00:19:43.260 --> 00:19:45.857
So if you blow a promise,
I don't want to hear,

00:19:45.857 --> 00:19:48.130
"Gary, I didn't what I
said 'cause you know,

00:19:48.130 --> 00:19:49.350
this happened and then this

00:19:49.350 --> 00:19:51.700
and they didn't return my email and then-"

00:19:51.700 --> 00:19:54.407
So there's no, there's just,

00:19:54.407 --> 00:19:57.150
"Hi. I know I said I would do that.

00:19:57.150 --> 00:19:59.170
I didn't do it.

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:01.350
That is clearly unacceptable.

00:20:01.350 --> 00:20:02.850
Here's what I'll do about it.

00:20:02.850 --> 00:20:04.640
Here's when it will be done.

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:05.805
And did I mess your-

00:20:05.805 --> 00:20:09.367
- Or feeling comfortable
in even saying, you know

00:20:09.367 --> 00:20:10.590
"I'm a little concerned that I'm not

00:20:10.590 --> 00:20:11.750
gonna be able to deliver on this."

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:12.700
- Exactly.

00:20:12.700 --> 00:20:17.260
On Wednesday before the
deliverable is due on Friday.

00:20:17.260 --> 00:20:20.590
Even though I know you're
hoping you will get it done

00:20:20.590 --> 00:20:22.180
and that you won't get in trouble.

00:20:22.180 --> 00:20:24.697
Well, no one then says on Wednesday,

00:20:24.697 --> 00:20:27.470
"Okay, listen. I'm a bit- I'm behind.

00:20:27.470 --> 00:20:28.330
A mess.

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:29.270
This is due Friday.

00:20:29.270 --> 00:20:30.570
It's not going to happen.

00:20:30.570 --> 00:20:32.410
Here's what I'm going to do about it.

00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:34.010
Did that mess you up?"

00:20:34.010 --> 00:20:34.843
Et cetera.

00:20:34.843 --> 00:20:38.470
So there's a language of
owning when you're not

00:20:38.470 --> 00:20:40.420
gonna do what you said.

00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:42.120
Even the CEO, Gary.

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:44.450
Every CEO is allowed to change their mind.

00:20:44.450 --> 00:20:45.283
You could have said-

00:20:45.283 --> 00:20:46.490
- I love changing my mind.

00:20:46.490 --> 00:20:48.389
- Right, I know you do, but you-

00:20:48.389 --> 00:20:50.379
(Beth laughs)

00:20:50.379 --> 00:20:51.370
- And I do, I mean-

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:55.250
- I know, but you have to be able to

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:58.130
own it rather than explain it

00:20:58.130 --> 00:20:59.280
'cause at the end of the day

00:20:59.280 --> 00:21:01.820
no one wants to friggin'
hear your explanation

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:04.340
about why you just freakin'
changed your mind again

00:21:04.340 --> 00:21:05.920
or not gonna do what you said.

00:21:05.920 --> 00:21:07.827
They just want to be able to hear,

00:21:07.827 --> 00:21:10.400
"Beth, listen. I know I told
you I was going to do that.

00:21:10.400 --> 00:21:11.940
Not going to do it.

00:21:11.940 --> 00:21:13.750
Now I know that messes with you

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:15.450
but here's what I'm gonna do about it."

00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:16.731
Boom, boom, boom.

00:21:16.731 --> 00:21:18.140
And then let them speak.

00:21:18.140 --> 00:21:20.040
So there's a language of accountability

00:21:20.040 --> 00:21:22.840
that's missing in most companies.

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:23.690
- Love that.

00:21:23.690 --> 00:21:26.440
Beth, how many people

00:21:26.440 --> 00:21:28.980
end up leaving companies that were

00:21:28.980 --> 00:21:30.940
actually good jobs for them

00:21:30.940 --> 00:21:33.090
strictly because they were unable

00:21:33.090 --> 00:21:35.620
to have the proper conversation?

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:39.280
You know, when I think about
all the people that have left,

00:21:39.280 --> 00:21:41.220
I get it on the receiving end.

00:21:41.220 --> 00:21:43.500
I get people that email
four or five years later

00:21:43.500 --> 00:21:46.130
that regret leaving because
they didn't take care

00:21:46.130 --> 00:21:49.010
of one little thing that
became a big thing, you know?

00:21:49.010 --> 00:21:50.790
And by the way, by the way,

00:21:50.790 --> 00:21:53.440
I have enough self-awareness
and accountability to know

00:21:53.440 --> 00:21:55.810
that if I didn't have the luxury

00:21:55.810 --> 00:22:00.540
